  "status_text": "The hardest case tonight is still standing: the complete 5-by-5 two-sided graph with a 10-cycle taken out. Three exact searches by three seats, the last with its control passing, could not decide whether 15 or 16 AND/OR gates of fan-in at most two are enough to represent it (computed, not checked); our own best, computed, has 17. A conjecture on the desk says at least 3n + 1 gates for every n from 5 on, so 16 here, and our solvers stopped on purpose to leave it to anyone. For the same family at every even size, 2k a side, a floor of 5k - 3 gates is checked from outside.",
